  "prefLabel": "Env-C 502.03 Business organization",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-C 502.03 “Business organization” means “business organization” as defined in RSA 310-A:2, I-a, namely “any enterprise, whether corporation, partnership, limited liability company, proprietorship, association, business trust, real estate trust, or other form of organization; organized for gain or profit, carrying on any business activity within the state.”\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-C 500) #10644, eff 7-22-14; ss by #14060, eff 8-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-c500.html"
